OL,3,GNEWSANo legal powers for Welsh Covid-19
OL,4,Areview, first minister says
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Welsh government's coronavirus
OL,7,Fpandemic review will not have statutory
OL,8,Fpowers to compel witnesses to give
OL,9,Fevidence, the first minister has
OL,10,Fconfirmed.
OL,12,FCampaigners representing families who
OL,13,Flost loved ones to Covid-19 have warned
OL,14,Fthey will not take part in a review
OL,15,Funable to require witnesses to give
OL,16,Fevidence under oath, something Plaid
OL,17,FCymru promised before entering
OL,18,Fgovernment.
OL,20,FRhun ap Iorwerth told S4C's Y Byd yn ei
OL,21,FLe programme the review "does not have
OL,22,Fthe same powers as a full inquiry".
OL,23,APub: 23-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
FL,439,430,260,140,0,100
